# scripts/complexity.allow - baseline ratchet of scripts/check-complexity.sh: the sites of each rule a file has today.
# Columns (tab-separated): RULE	PATH	COUNT	REASON
#   - foreach-node-raw never has a row (a hard zero).
#   - A new site, or a COUNT above the row, fails. A fixed site lowers the actual count under the row and fails too until the row is lowered or deleted,
#     so the list shrinks to zero. A new row is not the fix: the site gets the geometric growth, the cursor or the single sort.
#   - Rows are sorted by RULE, then PATH (LC_ALL=C). Refresh: scripts/check-complexity.sh --list > scripts/complexity.allow
